#import "../lib.typ": *

#recipe(
  minutes: 45,
)[
  == Palak Chicken

  Chicken in Indian-style spinach gravy. Great
  with basmati rice or naan.

  === Ingredients

  #ingredients[
    Marinade:

    - Chicken, boneless -- 500 g
    - Lemon juice -- 1 tbsp
    - Black pepper -- 1/4 tsp
    - Kashmiri or just red chili powder -- 1/4 tsp
    - Salt -- 1/4 tsp

    Spinach paste:

    - Baby spinach -- 250 g
    - Green chili -- 2-4 pc
    - Cashews -- 16 pc

    Gravy:

    - Vegetable oil -- 2 tbsp
    - Onion -- 1 pc
    - Tomato -- 1-2 pc or 1/2 cup canned tomatoes
    - Ginger garlic paste -- 2 tsp
    - Garam masala -- 1/2 tsp
    - Kasuri methi -- 1 tbsp
    - Salt -- 3/4 tsp
    - Cream ~ (optional) -- 1 tbsp

    Whole spices (optional):

    - Cumin seeds -- 1/2 tsp
    - Bay leaf -- 1 pc
    - Green cardamom -- 3 pc
    - Cloves -- 3 pc
    - Cinnamon -- 2 cm
  ]

  === Preparation

  + Chop the chicken into \~3 cm cubes and mix with the marinade ingredients.
    Set aside.
  + Heat up 1 tsp of oil in a pan, fry the cashews and green chilies until the
    chilies blister. Add the spinach and cook on medium for about 6 minutes
    until wilted. Let it cool.
  + Blend the spinach mix with 1/2 cup of cold water to a smooth paste.
  + Chop the onion and tomatoes finely.
  + Heat up the rest of the oil in a large pan, add the whole spices and let
    them sizzle. Add the onion and fry until soft and light brown.
  + Add the ginger garlic paste and fry for a minute. Then add the tomatoes and
    salt, and cook until they break down.
  + Add the chicken and fry on medium-high until pale, then stir in the garam
    masala. Add 1/2 cup of hot water, cover and cook until the chicken is done.
  + Stir in the spinach paste and simmer for 3--4 minutes. Add a splash of
    water if it is too thick.
  + Crush the kasuri methi between your palms and sprinkle over. Garnish with
    cream and a squeeze of lemon. Enjoy!
  + When you make the rice, be a good Asian and wash it first! If it's Basmati, ratio is 1:1.5, other rice is usually 1:2.
]
